test.yaml:7:13: startsWith(github.actor, "jdx") is also true for an account whose name only begins with "jdx", such as "jdx-evil", which anybody can create. compare the whole name with == or, for several names, test a list with contains(fromJSON('["a", "b"]'), value) [unsound-prefix-match]
test.yaml:9:13: endsWith(github.repository, "/mise") is also true for a fork of the repository by any owner, such as "evil/mise", which anybody can create. compare the whole name with == or, for several names, test a list with contains(fromJSON('["a", "b"]'), value) [unsound-prefix-match]
test.yaml:11:13: startsWith(github.repository, "jdx") is also true for a repository of an owner whose name only begins with "jdx", such as "jdx-evil/x", which anybody can create. end the prefix with a slash to match the owner, as in "jdx/", or compare the whole name with == or, for several names, test a list with contains(fromJSON('["a", "b"]'), value) [unsound-prefix-match]
test.yaml:14:22: contains(github.event.pull_request.user.login, "jdx") is also true for an account whose name only contains "jdx", which anybody can create. compare the whole name with == or, for several names, test a list with contains(fromJSON('["a", "b"]'), value) [unsound-prefix-match]
